{
  "version": "2026-10-03.1",
  "purpose": "Closed, hand-curated list of the sources a teaching line in Ludus may cite (CLAUDE.md TABOO 0.35 rule 18, TABOO 0.37). scripts/check_canon.py fails the build when a dialogue node, a passion or a confession question cites anything outside this list, a chapter or step that does not exist, a Synaxarion date that is not listed, or a topic that the cited step or chapter does not treat.",
  "rules": [
    "Only the chorus of 12 editors adds an entry, through a PR with the Theologian's verdict (TABOO 0.37).",
    "Kinds: scripture, father, council, canon-law, catechism, hagiography, synaxarion are authorities; witness is a historical or craft source that may support a line but never carries a teaching alone.",
    "A work of a non-Orthodox author after 1054 is only ever a witness.",
    "Chapter bounds are checked; verses are not (the checker says so and does not pretend otherwise).",
    "Russian abbreviations (Мф, Мк, Лк, Ин, Пс, Притч, Рим, Лествица, слово N, Достопамятные сказания) are aliases of the same entries, not new works. Patrologist of the chorus, 2026-10-03: prejudice 'the gate reads the English source, so the game is checked' / counter: the player reads the Russian copies (locations-99.json lesson, story-12.json goal) / why: the gate reads those copies against the same canon."
  ],
